WEBVTT

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.980
<i>It's a sunny Sunday.</i>

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:39.990
<i>Hinata's dad is giving us a ride 
to Gunma on his way to work.</i>

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.720
What are you reporting on today?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.500
I'm writing an article on Yamada Noboru-san.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.230
Yamada-san?

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.630
He's one of Gunma's greatest mountaineers,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.330
who conquered several 8,000 
meter-level mountains.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.260
Wow!

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.760
Can we read the book when it's done?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.820
Hey, do you think we'll get 
a view of Mt. Tanigawa?

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.230
We'll be off the highway soon.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.670
I don't think you'll see it.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:04.640
Aw...

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.600
<i>We're headed to Mt. Tanigawa, a mountain 
with a special place in our hearts...</i>

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.860
<i>Or rather, a castle.</i>

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.860
Japan's first restoration 
of a European castle

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.860
<b>Lockheart Castle</b>

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.520
<i>Lockheart Castle, a theme 
park of stone in Gunma.</i>

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.200
<i>Kaede-san had to stay behind 
to study with Yuka-san,</i>

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.380
<i>but Honoka-chan, who lives 
in Gunma, is joining us.</i>

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.710
Honoka-chan!

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.970
<b>Let's Photograph Our Memories!</b>

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.540
Okay, I'll come back for 
you in the evening.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.870
Thanks!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.770
Did you wait long?

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.200
Not really.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.360
I just got here.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.740
Did you come by bus?

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.240
No, Onii...

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.060
My brother gave me a ride.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:03.990
Let's go.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.860
Yes, let's go.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.000
I've always wanted to visit 
Lockheart Castle once.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.550
Kokona-chan told me about it.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.390
She said there's an amazing place here.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:18.050
They transported this castle 
straight from Scotland.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.490
I knew about this place, 
but I've never been here.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.260
I'm excited, too.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.550
Castle!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.170
Do you think we'll see a princess?

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.020
Of course not.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.190
A froggy!

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.160
It's so cute!

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:42.070
There's a hippo and a 
squirrel and a lion, too!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.950
Let's go over there.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.700
Power Stone
Granite

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.700
Touch with another person.
It will make you more emotionally 
developed and keep you earnest.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.700
Power Stone?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:53.920
Apparently it makes you more emotionally 
developed and keeps you earnest.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.590
It says to touch it with another person.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.340
Aren't you supposed to do 
this with your partner?

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.910
I feel like I've become 
more emotionally developed.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:02.970
Are you sure?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.380
Don't you feel it, Aoi-san?

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.050
Now that you mention it...

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:12.980
I feel like I have, or maybe not...

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.960
Help me, Aoi!

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.730
What did I do to deserve this?

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.240
No, save me!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.240
Let's leave Hinata-san behind.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.880
Let's have lunch before we go to the top.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.160
Yes, I'm starving.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.820
This looks delicious!

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.540
Time to eat!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.790
It's such a fancy curry.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.460
It's delicious.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.590
Oh, yeah!

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:45.220
Dad won this in a bingo game, 
and he gave it to me.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:47.740
Huh?

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.930
There's nothing showing on it.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.520
That's weird.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.020
The photo will show up if you wait for a bit.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.020
Really?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.590
Actually, I brought a camera, too.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.700
May I take a picture of you three?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.430
Sure.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.560
Okay!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.040
Here we go, then.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.210
Say cheese.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.930
How did it turn out?

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.340
Let me see.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.920
It's a film camera.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.070
We can't see it right away.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.050
Film?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.370
Unlike a digital camera,

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:30.300
you can't tell if you got a good picture 
or not until it's been developed.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.060
Wow, that's inconvenient.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.040
Nah.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.340
That's what makes it all the more fun.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.190
And you can only take so many pictures,

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.470
so each one becomes more precious.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.830
Yes.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:46.570
Let's take lots of memorable photos today.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:47.750
Yeah!

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.200
Um...

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.330
Yeah!

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:51.330
<b>Smartphone</b>

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.370
There are hearts everywhere.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.380
Because it's "Lockheart"?

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:02.590
Oh, is that what it is?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.210
I don't know, actually.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.890
Hey!

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.770
Get up here, Aoi!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.140
No way!

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.080
It's an actual castle!

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.670
Wow.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.470
Hey, a princess!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.430
I told you, there's no way there—

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.940
There is!

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.440
Beautiful!

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.310
Wh-What's this?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.970
<b>Become a Princess</b>

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.970
"Become a princess"!

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.080
Let's do it!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:58.600
Yes!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.020
Come on, let's go.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.680
H-Hey!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.360
Let's go, Honoka-san.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.010
Ta-da!

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.370
Jeez.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.870
It's like a dream.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.020
All right, let's take some pictures.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.650
Stand closer together, you two.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.590
L-Like this?

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.150
Closer!

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.040
Okay, say cheese.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.250
It's pretty dark.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.540
Don't you need to use the flash?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.310
This camera has a bright lens.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.160
It has a maximum aperture of f/2.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.420
f/2?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Maximum Aperture</b>

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:12.550
You can use a plenty fast shutter 
speed even when it's this dark.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Shutter Speed</b>

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.340
You don't need to raise the ISO much, either.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.430
It's saving in both JPEG and RAW format,

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.310
so you can adjust the exposure 
and white balance later, too.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Exposure</b>

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>White Balance</b>

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Aperture Priority</b>

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Depth of Field</b>

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.310
<b>Focal Length</b>

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.440
It's so pretty!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.850
I don't take many pictures of people,

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:34.200
but it's actually pretty fun.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.700
Okay, I'll take a picture of you now.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.640
I'll pass.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.420
Come on, don't say that.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.960
You don't often get a chance 
to become a princess.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.870
Honoka-chan, smile!

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:54.470
Honoka-san, is there a trick 
to taking portrait photos?

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.870
A trick?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:01.970
I guess it's to capture a natural image by 
taking it before the person gets tense.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.530
Got it.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.990
Look, a UFO!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.030
I don't see a UFO...

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.280
I got a good expression out of you.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.410
You got me.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.130
UFO? Where?

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.370
I have to get a picture!

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.440
<i>UFOs aside,</i>

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:32.430
<i>we took lots of pictures and enjoyed 
our day at Lockheart Castle.</i>

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.200
That was fun!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.550
I'm glad we came.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:40.410
Thanks for telling us about this 
beautiful place, Kokona-chan.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.510
My pleasure.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.770
What's up, Honoka-chan?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.060
Is your dad here yet, Hinata-chan?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.670
He just texted me, so I think 
he should be here soon.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.730
Why?

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.870
Why?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.740
<b>Lockheart</b>

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.740
I'm here, Honoka.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.870
Honoka-chan's brother?

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.170
<i>Man, he's so trashy.</i>

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.620
Thanks for taking care of Honoka.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.380
N-Not at all.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.990
That's an awesome car.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:19.930
Can you tell?

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.250
I just got it.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:24.350
It sounds badass, doesn't it?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.530
It has great suspension, too.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.470
That's enough. Just be quiet!

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:30.810
What's the matter, Honoka?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.950
You'd normally be like...

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:35.960
"Onii-chwan, thanks for coming to pick me up!"

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.070
And you'd hang all over me.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.950
I-I don't talk like that!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.820
Stop it, stupid!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.680
<i>A surprising side to Honoka-chan.</i>

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:45.680
Are you being shy?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:46.950
I'm not!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.570
Stop it!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.570
You're so cute.

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:53.340
W-Well, see you.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.000
Yeah.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.240
Let's hang out again!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:56.750
I'll send you the photos.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.960
I'll be waiting!

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:58.950
Shut up.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:02.090
Oh, come on, don't be so cold.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:12.380
I used up all the film.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:22.870
<i>When we got home, we had the film developed.</i>

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:26.440
<i>It's fun seeing photos 
on your phone or your PC,</i>

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:30.840
<i>but there's something nice about photos 
that you can physically touch, too.</i>

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.620
<i>Lots of fun memories.</i>

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.410
<i>I hope Honoka-chan appreciates them, too.</i>

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.010
Hinata Kokona

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.010
Aoi Honoka

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.600
To be continued.
